{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-9749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a series $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+⋯?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-9749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+⋯$ is the sum of a geometric series since the ratio of any two consecutive terms is constant.\n\nFirst, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $r=4.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{3}\\cdot ({4}^{N}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-9749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c6ac104dcb9781b4c3b3acc9bf630b159acf6b8425c8c55b7c69547e874bdec"} {"question" "q-9749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-9749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{6}(1-{4}^{N})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}+1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "{(\\frac{4}{6})}^{N}+\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "{(\\frac{4}{6})}^{N}-\\frac{1}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-9749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-39996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $3+15+75+⋯\\,?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-39996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=5.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{5}^{N})}{1-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{5}^{N})}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(1-{5}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({5}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-39996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c6ac104dcb9781b4c3b3acc9bf630b159acf6b8425c8c55b7c69547e874bdec"} {"question" "q-39996" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-39996" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}({5}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}(1-{5}^{N})"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}({5}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}(1-{3}^{N})"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}({3}^{N}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-39996" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}({5}^{N}-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-67104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $192$ and the common ratio is $4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-67104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 192 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 192 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{3(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(-3)}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =-(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & ={4}^{N}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-67104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c6ac104dcb9781b4c3b3acc9bf630b159acf6b8425c8c55b7c69547e874bdec"} {"question" "q-67104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-67104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3({4}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "4({3}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "{3}^{N}-1"] ["math" "{4}^{N}-1"] ["math" "{4}^{N}-12"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-67104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{4}^{N}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-73425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $384$ and the common ratio is $4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-73425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{3} \\\\ 384 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=6$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{6(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(-3)}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =-2(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =2({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-73425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c6ac104dcb9781b4c3b3acc9bf630b159acf6b8425c8c55b7c69547e874bdec"} {"question" "q-73425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-73425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({4}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "3({4}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "{4}^{N}-1"] ["math" "{4}^{N}-2"] ["math" "{4}^{N}-3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-73425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2({4}^{N}-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-276486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $320$ and the common ratio is $4?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-276486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 320 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 320 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(1-{4}^{N})}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}({4}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-276486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c6ac104dcb9781b4c3b3acc9bf630b159acf6b8425c8c55b7c69547e874bdec"} {"question" "q-276486" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"} {"question" "q-276486" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{3}(4^N-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064602/state.json" "file_sha256" "9170e231995d65fa3cc2f449fc8016aa3d5658dacf6ae66c7c7130171dedd467"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2113 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
